  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 721.12 Bottled Water and Point-of-Use or Point-of Entry Devices",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 721.12 Bottled Water and Point-of-Use or Point-of Entry Devices.\n\n(a) The department shall require a public water system to provide bottled water or point-of-use or point-of-entry devices or other means of response as a condition for granting an exemption from the requirements of Env-Dw 703 through Env-Dw 706.\n\n(b) The owner of a public water system that uses bottled water as a condition of obtaining an exemption shall ensure the bottled water source meets the requirements specified in Env-Dw 303.\n\n(c) The owner of a public water system that uses point-of-use or point-of-entry devices as a condition for receiving an exemption shall meet the requirements specified in Env-Dw 723.\n\nSource. #10617, eff 6-1-14",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
